  },
  "question": {
    "text": "A dc source of emf $\\mathrm{E}_1=100 \\mathrm{~V}$ and internal resistance $r=0.5 \\Omega$, a storage battery of emf $\\mathrm{E}_2=90 \\mathrm{~V}$ and an external resistance $\\mathrm{R}$ are connected as shown in figure. For what value of R no current will pass through the battery?\n<img src=\"assets\\qt0340_f941777c4c0a.png\"><br>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$5.5 \\Omega$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$3.5 \\Omega$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$4.5 \\Omega$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$2.5 \\Omega$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\frac{100}{R+r}=\\frac{90}{R}$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad \\frac{\\mathrm{R}+\\mathrm{r}}{\\mathrm{R}}=\\frac{10}{9} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad 1+\\frac{0.5}{\\mathrm{R}}=\\frac{10}{9} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad \\frac{0.5}{\\mathrm{R}}=\\frac{1}{9} \\\\\n& \\therefore \\mathrm{R}=4.5 \\Omega\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  }
}